This is an update to the initial attempt to port the distortion generator code to run on racf.

Some important notes:
- generate_distortion_map.C hard-codes rcorliss paths for the electric and magnetic fieldmaps, as well as for the directory containing greens functions for the Rossegger decomposition of the TPC interior.  If the latter file is not present for the specific binning requested, AnnularFieldSim will generate it.  At the default resolution settings, this single-threaded task takes about a day.  For the time being, Ross maintains this 1gb file, along with external E- and B- field maps in /sphenix/user/rcorliss/rossegger/.  
- This currently compiles, but there is a sporadic crash after the bulk of computation that can cause the distortion map .hist.root not to write correctly.
- Earlier versions required specific binning of the input histogram.  This version may behave poorly if the input histogram has much higher resolution than the output (namely, some bins may not be sampled, and hence sharp features may be lost), but will otherwise run fine.
- A prototype of a condor job file and submission script are also included.

To generate distortion maps:
  root -b -q ./generate_distortion_map.C\(\"$inputname\",\"$outputname\",\"$ibfname\",\"$primname\",1\)

where:
inputname = the full path to the spacecharge histogram file
outputname= the desired name of the output file, except for the extension, which will be added for various .root and .pdf monitoring plots
ibfname = the name of the ibf-only histogram inside the histogram file
ibfname = the name of the primaries-only histogram inside the histogram file
1 = a flag instructing the macro to use the provided spacecharge.  if false, the histograms must still exist, but they will not be processed.

See bash_for_condor_submission for an example of this.
